🚽 Test case: #193 -- nesting a call to the SAME struct-taking function as
🚽 one of its own arguments (`pick(pick(p, q), q)`) must bind parameters in
🚽 source order. enter_function_scope() used to reverse func->parameters in
🚽 place and then evaluate arguments (which re-enters that same list for the
🚽 inner call), binding the inner call's a/b swapped -- returning q (2)
🚽 instead of p (1). PR #254 snapshots the parameter order first, so the
🚽 inner pick returns its first argument p.
gang N {
    rizz v;
};

gang N pick(gang N a, gang N b) {
    bussin a;
}

skibidi main {
    gang N p;
    p.v = 1;
    gang N q;
    q.v = 2;
    gang N r = pick(pick(p, q), q);
    yapping("%d", r.v);
}
